      "writtenOn": "2021-06-24T04:21:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Can we fix the limitation\n\nDo you mean make Android start looking for the fstab in /etc/ and /first_stage_ramdisk/etc/, in addition to / and /first_stage_ramdisk/?  That would be possible, but it would increase the number of places that Android looks for the fstab from 4 to 6 (and actually 12 to 18 since there are 3 suffixes tried for each directory).  On one hand there is clearly a precedent of looking for the fstab in a lot of different places, but on the other it seems preferable to avoid making the problem worse.\n\n\u003e or use prebuilt_root module type for vendor ramdisk?\n\nDo you mean that for each fstab, a prebuilt_etc module would be used to install it to vendor/etc/, and a prebuilt_root module would be used to install it to vendor_ramdisk/first_stage_ramdisk/?  That might work, although I was hoping there would be an easier way to do it.  Keep in mind that fstabs are a per-device thing, so whatever the canonical way to install them is / will be, it has to be duplicated in every device directory.  What solution do you think should be used going forwards?",
      "parentUuid": "59ae03e6_d2fff146",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "ea7464aea2551ef7df2ba20300d0dac37f9461e3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c43c890a_01738366",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-25T10:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The init ramdisk is, AFAIK, is the only place where fstab is read from root. We can\u0027t deprecate the existing behavior easily, but I really think we should try to avoid putting things directly under root.\n\n/first_stage_ramdisk and / are actually the same directory. The only difference is whether the function is called before or after the chroot. So the order between the two doesn\u0027t really matter; both can\u0027t match at the same time. Therefore, I think it\u0027d be fine as long as we search [/first_stage_ramdisk]/etc directories after [/first_stage_ramdisk]/, for the compatibility with the legacy devices.\n\nAs a good side effect, this will help stop doing a trick like https://source.corp.google.com/android/packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid/Android.bp;rcl\u003dc9f6277d4cf29af64e890470b5f6fb860d8647ff;l\u003d274\n\n\u003e duplicated in every device directory\n\nIf you are going to replace PRODUCT_COPY_FILES with soong modules in every device, my second suggestion wouldn\u0027t be appealing. But if defining a canonical way is part of the (bigger) plan, I think it\u0027d be better to use this as a chance to fix the weirdness in fstab paths.\n\nLet me add Bowgo (who added /vendor/etc/fstab) and David who\u0027s owning init to hear their opinion about allowing \"\u003cpartition\u003e/etc/fstab.*\" also in the init ramdisk.",
      "parentUuid": "8ca72686_b8d02d56",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "ea7464aea2551ef7df2ba20300d0dac37f9461e3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
