      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1, I have similar thought as David. \n\nFeel free to clean it if there is a technical benefit.\n\nBtw, there is a symlink etc -\u003e system/etc in the root of system.img.\n\nIt might make the SwitchRoot(\"/system\"); fail if there is /etc/fstab.* in the ramdisk?\n\nhttp://cs/android/system/core/init/first_stage_mount.cpp?l\u003d528\u0026rcl\u003d1296b68869b3fc02daa9a8595846d312418bf4fc\n\nhttp://cs/android/system/core/init/switch_root.cpp?l\u003d80\u0026rcl\u003d1296b68869b3fc02daa9a8595846d312418bf4fc\n\nNote that a device also have a duplicated fstab file under /vendor/etc/fstab.*, because the ramdisk will be freed after init first stage. \n\nhttp://cs/android/system/core/init/first_stage_init.cpp?l\u003d60\u0026rcl\u003d1296b68869b3fc02daa9a8595846d312418bf4fc\n\nSome other mounts (e.g., /data) occurred in the second stage needs the /vendor/etc/fstab.* file for mounting.",
      "parentUuid": "6a2622d8_6fb67917",
